IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), s 201(12) to (15A) (Part 6, Division 1): when financial statements need not comply with the Accounting Standards,
-- what they must then contain, and the Minister's orders. Section 201 is the longest section of this part, so it is split in four modules:
--   sgc1-s201-departures.l4  (12) to (15A)        this module
--   sgc1-s201.l4             (1) to (11)          imports this module, for "Subject to subsections (12) to (15A)"
--   sgc1-s201-statement.l4   (16) to (23)         the directors' statement, reserves, banks, charities, savings
-- The power to make an order in the Gazette (subsections (15) and (15A)) is the Minister's and is not encoded; what an order means to a company
-- and its directors is. Whether an order exists is a fact the person states (the order is not among the sources).

§ `Section 201(12): approval of the Registrar to non-compliance`

-- src:18067 | (12) The financial statements or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18068 | of a company need not comply with all or any of the requirements of
-- src:18069 | the Accounting Standards for the purposes of subsection (1) or (5), if
-- src:18070 | the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to such
-- src:18071 | non‑compliance.
@ref s 201(12) (src:18067-18071)
GIVEN `the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to the non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(12) the financial statements need not comply with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` MEANS
    IF `the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to the non-compliance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not comply with all or any of the requirements of the Accounting Standards ... if the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to such non-compliance" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a), NOTES.md; the other reading is NOTHING, since the relief is grant-like)

§ `Section 201(13): the true and fair view override`

-- src:18077 | (13) Where financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18078 | statements prepared in accordance with any requirement of the
-- src:18079 | Accounting Standards for the purposes of subsection (1) or (5), would
-- src:18080 | not give a true and fair view of any matter required by this section to
-- src:18081 | be dealt with in the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18082 | statements, the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18083 | statements need not comply with that requirement to the extent that
-- src:18084 | this is necessary for them to give a true and fair view of the matter.
@ref s 201(13) (src:18077-18084)
GIVEN `financial statements prepared in accordance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards would not give a true and fair view of a matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not complying with that requirement is necessary for the financial statements to give a true and fair view of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(13) the financial statements need not comply with the requirement of the Accounting Standards` MEANS
    IF    `financial statements prepared in accordance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards would not give a true and fair view of a matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them`
       AND `not complying with that requirement is necessary for the financial statements to give a true and fair view of the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where financial statements ... prepared in accordance with any requirement of the Accounting Standards ... would not give a true and fair view of any matter ..., the financial statements ... need not comply with that requirement to the extent that this is necessary for them to give a true and fair view of the matter" (a failed "where", the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); and a limit "to the extent that this is necessary")

§ `Section 201(14): what the financial statements must then include`

-- src:18088 | (14) In the event of any non‑compliance with a requirement of the
-- src:18089 | Accounting Standards mentioned in subsection (13), there must be
-- src:18090 | included in the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18091 | statements, as the case may be —
-- src:18093 | (a) a statement by the auditor of the company that the auditor
-- src:18094 | agrees that such non‑compliance is necessary for the
-- src:18095 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18100 | (as the case may be) to give a true and fair view of the
-- src:18101 | matter concerned;
-- src:18103 | (b) particulars of the departure, the reason therefor and its
-- src:18104 | effect, if any; and
-- src:18106 | (c) such further information and explanations as will give a
-- src:18107 | true and fair view of that matter.
@ref s 201(14) (src:18088-18107)
GIVEN `there is a non-compliance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards of the kind subsection (13) mentions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(14) the financial statements must include the statement, particulars and information the subsection lists` MEANS
    IF `there is a non-compliance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards of the kind subsection (13) mentions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of any non-compliance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards mentioned in subsection (13), there must be included ..." (a failed "in the event of", read as "if": marginal reading (a))

@ref s 201(14) (src:18088-18107)
GIVEN `there is a non-compliance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards of the kind subsection (13) mentions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement by the auditor of the company that the auditor agrees that the non-compliance is necessary for the financial statements to give a true and fair view of the matter concerned is included` IS A BOOLEAN
      `particulars of the departure, the reason for it and its effect, if any, are included` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such further information and explanations as will give a true and fair view of the matter are included` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(14) the financial statements include what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `there is a non-compliance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards of the kind subsection (13) mentions`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only "in the event of any non-compliance ... mentioned in subsection (13)" and is silent on financial statements with no such non-compliance
    ELSE IF    `a statement by the auditor of the company that the auditor agrees that the non-compliance is necessary for the financial statements to give a true and fair view of the matter concerned is included`
            AND `particulars of the departure, the reason for it and its effect, if any, are included`
            AND `such further information and explanations as will give a true and fair view of the matter are included`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there must be included in the financial statements or consolidated financial statements, as the case may be — (a) a statement by the auditor ...; (b) particulars of the departure, the reason therefor and its effect, if any; and (c) such further information and explanations" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Section 201(15): the Minister's substitution of accounting standards`

-- src:18111 | (15) The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, in respect of
-- src:18112 | companies of a specified class or description, substitute the whole or
-- src:18113 | any part of other accounting standards specified in the order for the
-- src:18114 | whole or any part of the Accounting Standards, as specified in the
-- src:18115 | order, and the provisions of this section and sections 207 and 209A
-- src:18116 | apply accordingly in respect of such companies.
@ref s 201(15) (src:18111-18116)
GIVEN `an order in the Gazette substitutes other accounting standards for the Accounting Standards, in whole or in part, for companies of a class or description to which the company belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(15) the substituted standards apply to the company in place of the Accounting Standards` MEANS
    IF `an order in the Gazette substitutes other accounting standards for the Accounting Standards, in whole or in part, for companies of a class or description to which the company belongs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, in respect of companies of a specified class or description, substitute ..." (the only route the subsection gives is an order; the person states whether one applies to the company, as the order itself is not among the sources: marginal reading (a), NOTES.md; the other reading is NOTHING, pointing outside the text)

§ `Section 201(15A): the Minister's exemption of directors`

-- src:18120 | (15A) The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, exempt the
-- src:18121 | directors of any company that belongs to a specified class or
-- src:18122 | description of companies, from having to ensure that the company’s
-- src:18123 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements comply with
-- src:18124 | all or any of the requirements of the Accounting Standards specified
-- src:18125 | in the order.
@ref s 201(15A) (src:18120-18125)
GIVEN `an order in the Gazette exempts the directors of companies of a class or description to which the company belongs from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(15A) the directors are exempt from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement` MEANS
    IF `an order in the Gazette exempts the directors of companies of a class or description to which the company belongs from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, exempt the directors of any company that belongs to a specified class or description of companies" (the only route the subsection gives is an order; the person states whether one applies to the company, as the order itself is not among the sources: marginal reading (a), NOTES.md; the other reading is NOTHING, pointing outside the text)

§ `Subsections (12) to (15A) together: the "Subject to" of subsections (2) and (5)`

-- Subsections (2) and (5) are each "Subject to subsections (12) to (15A)". This is the one question they put to those subsections:
-- is the departure from the Accounting Standards one that (12), (13) or (15A) allows? (Subsection (15) changes the standards themselves; subsection (14) says what a departure must carry.)
-- Not a rule of its own: it calls the three functions above. JUST TRUE if any says yes; JUST FALSE if all three say no.
-- src:18067 | (12) The financial statements or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18068 | of a company need not comply with all or any of the requirements of
-- src:18069 | the Accounting Standards for the purposes of subsection (1) or (5), if
-- src:18070 | the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to such
-- src:18071 | non‑compliance.
-- src:18077 | (13) Where financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18078 | statements prepared in accordance with any requirement of the
-- src:18079 | Accounting Standards for the purposes of subsection (1) or (5), would
-- src:18080 | not give a true and fair view of any matter required by this section to
-- src:18081 | be dealt with in the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18082 | statements, the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18083 | statements need not comply with that requirement to the extent that
-- src:18084 | this is necessary for them to give a true and fair view of the matter.
-- src:18120 | (15A) The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, exempt the
-- src:18121 | directors of any company that belongs to a specified class or
-- src:18122 | description of companies, from having to ensure that the company’s
-- src:18123 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements comply with
-- src:18124 | all or any of the requirements of the Accounting Standards specified
-- src:18125 | in the order.
@ref s 201(12), (13) and (15A) (src:18067-18125)
GIVEN `the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to the non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `financial statements prepared in accordance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards would not give a true and fair view of a matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not complying with that requirement is necessary for the financial statements to give a true and fair view of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order in the Gazette exempts the directors of companies of a class or description to which the company belongs from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(12), (13) and (15A) a departure from the Accounting Standards is allowed` MEANS
    IF    `s 201(12) the financial statements need not comply with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` `the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar to the non-compliance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 201(13) the financial statements need not comply with the requirement of the Accounting Standards` `financial statements prepared in accordance with a requirement of the Accounting Standards would not give a true and fair view of a matter required by section 201 to be dealt with in them` `not complying with that requirement is necessary for the financial statements to give a true and fair view of the matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 201(15A) the directors are exempt from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement` `an order in the Gazette exempts the directors of companies of a class or description to which the company belongs from having to ensure that the financial statements comply with the requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not comply with all or any of the requirements of the Accounting Standards ... if the company has obtained the approval of the Registrar" (subsection (12), and likewise (13) and (15A): none of the three allows the departure on these facts; a combination of the three, not a rule of its own)
